{
  "requirement": "The `trust-but-verify` crate's `outline` module provides language selection,\nsource outlining, selector resolution, and source structural hashes.\nApplications can use these operations directly on files and supplied source\nsnapshots.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement says the `outline` module provides four things: language selection, source outlining, selector resolution and source structural hashes. It also says applications can use them directly on files and on supplied source snapshots. The three marked tests cover each of these through the public `trust_but_verify::outline` API (`OutlineContent`, `OutlineId`, `OutlineLang`, `languages`).\n\n- **Files and snapshots, with inferred language.** `fn[file_constructors_infer_the_language_and_return_addressed_contents]` writes `AUTH.RS` to disk. It builds contents with `OutlineContent::from_path` and `OutlineContent::from_source` from the same text. It asserts that:\n  - the language is inferred from the uppercase extension, via the `rust-structural-v1` scheme;\n  - the outline items are `\"\"` and `fn[check_token]`;\n  - the file and snapshot paths give equal fingerprints.\n- **Selector resolution.** The same test resolves `fn[check_token]` with `OutlineContent::from_id`, with `select` on the file-derived contents, and with `select` on the snapshot-derived contents. It asserts the selected text and that all three fingerprints are equal.\n- **Language selection and outlining across bundled languages.** `fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` runs a generic check over Rust, Python, TypeScript, Tsx, Markdown, Css, Toml and Yaml. For each language it asserts that:\n  - extension-based inference and an explicit `from_source_with` give identical selectors, diagnostics and fingerprints;\n  - the extension list, matched case-insensitively, and the fingerprint scheme are as expected;\n  - the root span covers the whole source and the expected selector resolves;\n  - `search_structure` returns ranges inside the source.\n  \n  It also checks that `PlainText` is named `plain-text` and claims no extensions.\n- **Structural hashes and snapshot semantics.** `fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` asserts that `structural_hash` and `fingerprint_scheme` match the fingerprint. It also asserts that a selected content keeps its text and fingerprint after the original handle is dropped and the file is edited. A later `from_id` on the edited file fails, while the retained contents can still `select(\"\")` the root.\n\nThe explicit-language file path, `from_path_with`, is exercised in `fn[explicit_languages_share_configuration_and_retain_their_scheme]`. That test is not marked for this requirement, but the requirement does not need it separately because the marked tests already show language selection and snapshot use. I found no uncovered obligation and no plausible violating behavior that these assertions would accept. There are no acknowledgments to assess.",
  "references": "78ca978244e2c786214b03a4a7b5167bf3ee1e90e18026fc67d7299357660038",
